Z||000000||Fiero54||05-21-2001||10:08 AM||||I was driving my 85GT last night and my tach went dead,it would work for like 2-3 seconds and then go dead again. Just wondering if any one has had a similar problem and if anyone would how to fix it.  Thank you for your help. ||||reg||13
Z||000001||TheFiero64||05-21-2001||10:49 AM||||Check the tach filter, it is a little tube next to the coil with 2 white wires coming out of it. Rodney Dickman sells a replacement if that is whats gone <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Fiero54||05-21-2001||11:52 AM||||Can you use a tach filter form a L4 for a V6?||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||05-21-2001||05:44 PM||||Yes you can. They're the same filter.||||reg||1
